mutant: m066_seal_reverses_block_order
target: internal/catalog/scripts.go
failure-mode: |
  The seal transaction writes the generation's block rows in reverse
  ordinal order while the footer lists the blocks in seq order, so the
  sealed generation maps each footer block to another block's object.
  Readers of the sealed segment fetch the wrong bytes for a seq range.
expected-detection: |
  Every full seed seals at least one segment. The layer 3 oracle downloads
  each pod's archive and compares it with the model, and it replays the
  sealed range to its observers; the reordered objects fail a decode check
  or deliver events out of order.
expected-tier: disagg
tiers: disagg

